{"id":"mahabharata-7-096","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":96,"title":"षण्णवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 96 · Satyaki breaks through to Arjuna","summary":{"en":"After defeating the Yavanas and Kambojas, Satyaki drives through the middle of the army, and Shakuni, Duhsaha and others strike at him together. He answers the great host with arrows and presses on.","kn":"ಯವನ, ಕಾಂಬೋಜರನ್ನು ಗೆದ್ದ ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಸೈನ್ಯದ ನಡುವೆ ಹಾದು ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಶಕುನಿ, ದುಃಸಹ ಮೊದಲಾದವರು ಒಟ್ಟಾಗಿ ಹೊಡೆಯುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅವನು ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಮಹಾಸೈನ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"यवनों और काम्बोजों को हराकर सात्यकि सेना के बीच से निकलता है, और शकुनि, दुःसह आदि मिलकर उस पर प्रहार करते हैं। वह बाणों से विशाल सेना को उत्तर देता है और आगे बढ़ता है।","te":"యవనులను, కాంభోజులను ఓడించిన సాత్యకి సేన మధ్య నుండి సాగుతాడు; శకుని, దుస్సహుడు తదితరులు కలిసి కొడతారు. బాణాలతో మహాసేనకు బదులిచ్చి ముందుకు సాగుతాడు.","ta":"யவனரையும் காம்போஜரையும் வென்ற சாத்யகி படையின் நடுவே செல்ல, சகுனி, துச்சகன் முதலியோர் சேர்ந்து தாக்குகின்றனர். அவன் அம்புகளால் பெரும்படைக்குப் பதிலளித்து முன்னேறுகிறான்.","ml":"യവനരെയും കംബോജരെയും പരാജയപ്പെടുത്തിയശേഷം സാത്യകി സേനയുടെ നടുവിലൂടെ തേര് തെളിക്കുന്നു; ശകുനിയും ദുസ്സഹനും മറ്റുള്ളവരും ഒന്നിച്ച് അദ്ദേഹത്തെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു. മഹാസേനയെ അമ്പുകൾകൊണ്ട് നേരിട്ട് അദ്ദേഹം മുന്നോട്ടു പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.96; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"जित्वा यवनकाम्बोजान्युयुधानस्ततोऽर्जुनम् ।\nजगाम तव सैन्यस्य मध्येन रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having defeated the Yavanas and Kambojas, Yuyudhana, best of charioteers, then went through the middle of your army toward Arjuna."}},{"n":2,"text":"शरदंष्ट्रो नरव्याघ्रो विचित्रकवचच्छविः ।\nमृगान्व्याघ्र इवाजिघ्रंस्तव सैन्यमभीषयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That tiger among men, whose arrows were his fangs and whose armor shone in many colors, frightened your army like a tiger scenting deer."}},{"n":3,"text":"स रथेन चरन्मार्गान्धनुरभ्रामयद्भृशम् ।\nरुक्मपृष्ठं महावेगं रुक्मचन्द्रकसंकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ranging about in his chariot, he whirled his gold-backed bow of great speed, ringed with golden moons."}},{"n":4,"text":"रुक्माङ्गदशिरस्त्राणो रुक्मवर्मसमावृतः ।\nरुक्मध्वजवरः शूरो मेरुशृङ्ग इवाबभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a golden armlet and helmet, wrapped in golden armor, with a fine golden banner, the hero shone like the peak of Meru."}},{"n":5,"text":"सधनुर्मण्डलः संख्ये तेजोभास्वररश्मिवान् ।\nशरदीवोदितः सूर्यो नृसूर्यो विरराज ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the circle of his bow in battle, like a bright sun with rays of splendor, that sun among men shone like the autumn sun risen."}},{"n":6,"text":"वृषभस्कन्धविक्रान्तो वृषभाक्षो नरर्षभः ।\nतावकानां बभौ मध्ये गवां मध्ये यथा वृषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the valor of a bull's shoulder and bull-like eyes, that bull among men shone amid your troops like a bull among cows."}},{"n":7,"text":"मत्तद्विरदसंकाशं मत्तद्विरदगामिनम् ।\nप्रभिन्नमिव मातङ्गं यूथमध्ये व्यवस्थितम् ।\nव्याघ्रा इव जिघांसन्तस्त्वदीयाभ्यद्रवन्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a rutting elephant in appearance and in gait, like a maddened tusker standing amid a herd, he was attacked in battle by your men, like tigers wishing to kill."}},{"n":8,"text":"द्रोणानीकमतिक्रान्तं भोजानीकं च दुस्तरम् ।\nजलसंधार्णवं तीर्त्वा काम्बोजानां च वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having passed Drona's host and the hard-to-cross Bhoja host, having crossed the ocean of Jalasandha and the Kamboja army,"}},{"n":9,"text":"हार्दिक्यमकरान्मुक्तं तीर्णं वै सैन्यसागरम् ।\nपरिवव्रुः सुसंक्रुद्धास्त्वदीयाः सात्यकिं रथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having crossed that sea of an army freed from the Hridika's-son crocodile, Satyaki was surrounded by your chariot-warriors, greatly enraged."}},{"n":10,"text":"दुर्योधनश्चित्रसेनो दुःशासनविविंशती ।\nशकुनिर्दुःसहश्चैव युवा दुर्मर्षणः क्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, Chitrasena, Duhshasana and Vivimshati, Shakuni, Duhsaha, the young Durmarshana and Kratha,"}},{"n":11,"text":"अन्ये च बहवः शूराः शस्त्रवन्तो दुरासदाः ।\nपृष्ठतः सात्यकिं यान्तमन्वधावन्नमर्षिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And many other brave armed warriors, hard to approach, in anger ran after Satyaki as he went."}},{"n":12,"text":"अथ शब्दो महानासीत्तव सैन्यस्य मारिष ।\nमारुतोद्धूतवेगस्य सागरस्येव पर्वणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a great din arose from your army, my lord, like the sea at the full moon driven by a wind."}},{"n":13,"text":"तानभिद्रवतः सर्वान्समीक्ष्य शिनिपुंगवः ।\nशनैर्याहीति यन्तारमब्रवीत्प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them all rushing at him, the bull of the Shinis, almost laughing, said to his charioteer, \"Go slowly.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"इदमेति समुद्धूतं धार्तराष्ट्रस्य यद्बलम् ।\nमामेवाभिमुखं तूर्णं गजाश्वरथपत्तिमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This Dhritarashtra's force that has risen up comes quickly at me alone, with elephants, horses, chariots and foot soldiers,"}},{"n":15,"text":"नादयन्वै दिशः सर्वा रथघोषेण सारथे ।\nपृथिवीं चान्तरिक्षं च कम्पयन्सागरानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Filling all the quarters with the rattle of chariots, charioteer, shaking earth and sky and even the oceans."}},{"n":16,"text":"एतद्बलार्णवं तात वारयिष्ये महारणे ।\nपौर्णमास्यामिवोद्धूतं वेलेव सलिलाशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall hold back this ocean of an army in the great battle, as the shore holds back the sea when it surges at the full moon."}},{"n":17,"text":"पश्य मे सूत विक्रान्तमिन्द्रस्येव महामृधे ।\nएष सैन्यानि शत्रूणां विधमामि शितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Charioteer, see my valor in this great battle, like Indra's. Here I destroy the enemy armies with sharp arrows."}},{"n":18,"text":"निहतानाहवे पश्य पदात्यश्वरथद्विपान् ।\nमच्छरैरग्निसंकाशैर्विदेहासून्सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"See foot soldiers, horses, chariots and elephants slain in the fight, and thousands of bodies deprived of life by my fiery arrows.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"इत्येवं ब्रुवतस्तस्य सात्यकेरमितौजसः ।\nसमीपं सैनिकास्ते तु शीघ्रमीयुर्युयुत्सवः ।\nजह्याद्रवस्व तिष्ठेति पश्य पश्येति वादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Satyaki of boundless might was speaking so, those soldiers eager to fight quickly came near, shouting, \"Kill him! Run! Stand! Look, look!\""}},{"n":20,"text":"तानेवं ब्रुवतो वीरान्सात्यकिर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nजघान त्रिशतानश्वान्कुञ्जरांश्च चतुःशतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As those heroes spoke so, Satyaki with sharp arrows killed three hundred horses and four hundred elephants."}},{"n":21,"text":"स संप्रहारस्तुमुलस्तस्य तेषां च धन्विनाम् ।\nदेवासुररणप्रख्यः प्रावर्तत जनक्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That tumultuous clash between him and those archers, which destroyed many men, was like the battle of the gods and asuras."}},{"n":22,"text":"मेघजालनिभं सैन्यं तव पुत्रस्य मारिष ।\nप्रत्यगृह्णाच्छिनेः पौत्रः शरैराशीविषोपमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The grandson of Shini met your son's army, like a mass of clouds, with arrows like venomous snakes."}},{"n":23,"text":"प्रच्छाद्यमानः समरे शरजालैः स वीर्यवान् ।\nअसंभ्रमं महाराज तावकानवधीद्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Covered in the battle by nets of arrows, the mighty one, without flurry, killed many of your men, great king."}},{"n":24,"text":"आश्चर्यं तत्र राजेन्द्र सुमहद्दृष्टवानहम् ।\nन मोघः सायकः कश्चित्सात्यकेरभवत्प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, O king of kings, I saw a great marvel: not one arrow of Satyaki's was wasted, my lord."}},{"n":25,"text":"रथनागाश्वकलिलः पदात्यूर्मिसमाकुलः ।\nशैनेयवेलामासाद्य स्थितः सैन्यमहार्णवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great ocean of an army, crowded with chariots, elephants and horses and rippled with foot soldiers, reached the shore that was Shaineya and stopped."}},{"n":26,"text":"संभ्रान्तनरनागाश्वमावर्तत मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nतत्सैन्यमिषुभिस्तेन वध्यमानं समन्ततः ।\nबभ्राम तत्र तत्रैव गावः शीतार्दिता इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"That army, its men, elephants and horses bewildered, kept whirling round and round, struck on all sides by his arrows, and wandered about right there like cows tormented by cold."}},{"n":27,"text":"पदातिनं रथं नागं सादिनं तुरगं तथा ।\nअविद्धं तत्र नाद्राक्षं युयुधानस्य सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I saw no foot soldier, chariot, elephant, rider or horse there unpierced by Yuyudhana's arrows."}},{"n":28,"text":"न तादृक्कदनं राजन्कृतवांस्तत्र फल्गुनः ।\nयादृक्क्षयमनीकानामकरोत्सात्यकिर्नृप ।\nअत्यर्जुनं शिनेः पौत्रो युध्यते भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Phalguna did not make such a slaughter there, O king, as Satyaki made of your armies; the grandson of Shini fought beyond Arjuna, O bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा सात्वतस्य त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nविव्याध सूतं निशितैश्चतुर्भिश्चतुरो हयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana struck the Satvata's charioteer with three arrows and his four horses with four sharp arrows."}},{"n":30,"text":"सात्यकिं च त्रिभिर्विद्ध्वा पुनर्विव्याध सोऽष्टभिः ।\nदुःशासनः षोडशभिर्विव्याध शिनिपुंगवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having struck Satyaki with three, he struck him again with eight. Duhshasana struck the bull of the Shinis with sixteen."}},{"n":31,"text":"शकुनिः पञ्चविंशत्या चित्रसेनश्च पञ्चभिः ।\nदुःसहः पञ्चदशभिर्विव्याधोरसि सात्यकिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni struck him with twenty-five, Chitrasena with five, and Duhsaha with fifteen in the chest."}},{"n":32,"text":"उत्स्मयन्वृष्णिशार्दूलस्तथा बाणैः समाहतः ।\nतानविध्यन्महाराज सर्वानेव त्रिभिस्त्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Smiling, the tiger of the Vrishnis, though struck by these arrows, pierced each one of them with three."}},{"n":33,"text":"गाढविद्धानरीन्कृत्वा मार्गणैः सोऽतितेजनैः ।\nशैनेयः श्येनवत्संख्ये व्यचरल्लघुविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having wounded his enemies deeply with extremely keen arrows, Shaineya ranged the battle like a falcon, light in his valor."}},{"n":34,"text":"सौबलस्य धनुश्छित्त्वा हस्तावापं निकृत्य च ।\nदुर्योधनं त्रिभिर्बाणैरभ्यविध्यत्स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"He cut Shakuni's bow and sliced off his hand-guard, and struck Duryodhana between the breasts with three arrows."}},{"n":35,"text":"चित्रसेनं शतेनैव दशभिर्दुःसहं तथा ।\nदुःशासनं च विंशत्या विव्याध शिनिपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Chitrasena with a hundred, Duhsaha with ten, and Duhshasana with twenty, that bull of the Shinis."}},{"n":36,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय स्यालस्तव विशां पते ।\nअष्टभिः सात्यकिं विद्ध्वा पुनर्विव्याध पञ्चभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your brother-in-law Shakuni, O lord of the people, took another bow and, having struck Satyaki with eight, struck him again with five."}},{"n":37,"text":"दुःशासनश्च दशभिर्दुःसहश्च त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nदुर्मुखश्च द्वादशभी राजन्विव्याध सात्यकिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana struck Satyaki with ten, Duhsaha with three arrows, and Durmukha, O king, with twelve."}},{"n":38,"text":"दुर्योधनस्त्रिसप्तत्या विद्ध्वा भारत माधवम् ।\nततोऽस्य निशितैर्बाणैस्त्रिभिर्विव्याध सारथिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, having struck the Madhava with seventy-three, O Bharata, then struck his charioteer with three sharp arrows."}},{"n":39,"text":"तान्सर्वान्सहिताञ्शूरान्यतमानान्महारथान् ।\nपञ्चभिः पञ्चभिर्बाणैः पुनर्विव्याध सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki again struck all those brave great chariot-warriors, striving together, with five arrows each."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततः स रथिनां श्रेष्ठस्तव पुत्रस्य सारथिम् ।\nआजघानाशु भल्लेन स हतो न्यपतद्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that best of charioteers quickly struck your son's charioteer with a broad-headed arrow, and he fell dead to the ground."}},{"n":41,"text":"पातिते सारथौ तस्मिंस्तव पुत्ररथः प्रभो ।\nवातायमानैस्तैरश्वैरपानीयत संगरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that charioteer fell, my lord, your son's chariot was carried out of the fight by its horses, swift as wind."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततस्तव सुता राजन्सैनिकाश्च विशां पते ।\nराज्ञो रथमभिप्रेक्ष्य विद्रुताः शतशोऽभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your sons, O king, and the soldiers, seeing the king's chariot, fled by the hundreds."}},{"n":43,"text":"विद्रुतं तत्र तत्सैन्यं दृष्ट्वा भारत सात्यकिः ।\nअवाकिरच्छरैस्तीक्ष्णै रुक्मपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that army fleeing, Bharata, Satyaki covered it with sharp, stone-whetted, gold-feathered arrows."}},{"n":44,"text":"विद्राव्य सर्वसैन्यानि तावकानि समन्ततः ।\nप्रययौ सात्यकी राजञ्श्वेताश्वस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having routed all your armies on every side, Satyaki went on, O king, toward the chariot of the white-horsed one."}},{"n":45,"text":"तं शरानाददानं च रक्षमाणं च सारथिम् ।\nआत्मानं मोचयन्तं च तावकाः समपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your own men honored him as he took up arrows, protected his charioteer and freed himself."}}]}]}